  "connectionProblemUserInfo": "The address must not carry a user or a password.",
  "@connectionProblemUserInfo": {"description": "Why the address cannot be saved"},
  "connectionHelpOpen": "Help about the server address",
  "@connectionHelpOpen": {"description": "Tooltip of the help of the address screen"},
  "connectionHelpBody": "The app reaches your server through one address, and everything goes through it: the API, the live connection and the login. Internal is the address on your network; external is the one on the internet, when your server is exposed; other is any address you type. Only https:// is accepted, except for localhost. Test the connection before saving: it asks the server and its login, and says which one did not answer. Your choice stays on this phone through restarts and sign-outs. Changing it ends your login, because the next one is with the server at the new address. This screen opens without signing in, from the sign-in screen, so a wrong address never locks you out.",
  "@connectionHelpBody": {"description": "Help of the address screen"},
